(Plan 291 Finding 5: `but if` conditional sugar generalized to `append`.
Base statement carries its own target `to line`; the branch reuses it.
Exercise both branches of the condition against separate buffers.)

a buffer called hit is 256 bytes in size.
a number called v1 is 1.
Append "." to hit, but if v1 is equal to 1 append "#".
Print hit.

a buffer called miss is 256 bytes in size.
a number called v2 is 2.
Append "." to miss, but if v2 is equal to 1 append "#".
Print miss.
